Native files (allowed scope: apps/apple/TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/BatteryHealthAnalyticsWidget.*):
  BatteryHealthAnalyticsWidget.swift          — SwiftUI surface: header + loading/empty/error/content,
                                                compact (cols<=1, gauge-only) vs standard (gauge + stats)
  BatteryHealthAnalyticsWidget.Model.swift    — P1/S8 state-holder seam, DTO, FormatPrefs, @Observable
                                                model, P1/S11 telemetry seam, registry, P1/S10 i18n facade
  BatteryHealthAnalyticsWidget.Adapter.swift  — pure projector (DTO→projection): scoreColor bands,
                                                grouped fmtInt/fmtNumber + gauge fmtNumber readout, a11y
  BatteryHealthAnalyticsWidget.Views.swift    — BatteryHealthRadialGauge (←web RadialGauge),
                                                BatteryHealthStatCluster (←WidgetGaugeHero stats),
                                                loading skeleton, connectivity banner, band→colour
  BatteryHealthAnalyticsWidget.Previews.swift — per-state + per-size #Previews (DEBUG only)
  BatteryHealthAnalyticsWidget.strings        — P1/S10 catalog contribution (table "BatteryHealthAnalyticsWidget")
  BatteryHealthAnalyticsWidget.Tests.swift    — adapter + format + phase + model + telemetry + registry + a11y

Data binds via the shared P1/S8 `BatteryHealthAnalyticsWidgetSource` seam (the production app wires the
`VehicleStore` active vehicle + the battery-health `Resource` + `SettingsStore`; previews/tests use the
in-memory source). No HTTP in the view. Web hooks reproduced: useVehicles (vid = vehicleId ?? vehicles[0].id),
useBatteryHealthAnalytics (GET /analytics/battery-health?vehicle_id=), useUnits, useTranslation.

useUnits note (no silent drift): the web source imports a temperature converter but the rendered output
reads only scores + percentages (no temperature is displayed — the `toTemperatureDisplay`/`tempUnit`
values are computed but never used in any stat). The observable effect of useUnits here is the
locale + precision applied by fmtNumber, which the native FormatPrefs seam carries. No temperature
conversion is fabricated.

Score bands ported verbatim from the web `scoreColor`: >=80 good #10b981, >=50 fair #f59e0b, else poor
#ef4444. Gauge readout = fmtNumber(clamped 0..100, integer→0 / else precision) + unit "health"; the
integer score sub-label below the ring = fmtInt(current_soh). Six stats — every value fmtInt /
fmtNumber(_,0) (grouped), `?? 0` fallbacks, web order + units:
  Cycles(total_cycles, —), Charge Depth(full_charge_pct, %), Discharge(avg_depth_of_discharge, %),
  DC Fast(fast_charge_pct, %), Temp Score(temp_exposure_score, "/ 100"), Habits(charge_habits_score, "/ 100").

States reproduced from the web source (every state renders — no hidden surface):
  loading (skeleton), empty ("No battery health data", HeartPulse→SF `waveform.path.ecg`),
  error (retry affordance), stale (chip + retained gauge, auto-refresh), offline (chip + cached gauge),
  content (gauge hero + six-stat cluster). isCompact = size.cols <= 1 drops title/icon + stats.

Registry (canonical registry/battery.ts → "battery-health-analytics"): name "Battery Analytics",
category `battery`, default 2×4, min 1×2, max 4×40 — registered with the same id + size envelope and
verified by the registry test (clamp honours 1×2 … 4×40).

i18n keys (all from source, resolved through the P1/S10 facade; no English literals in code):
  widget.batteryHealthAnalytics.{title,score,totalCycles,avgChargeDepth,avgDischargeDepth,dcFastRatio,
  tempExposure,chargeHabits,noData} + description; the stat unit glyphs (percentUnit/outOfHundred); plus
  native chrome (live/stale/offline/refresh/retry/loading/emptyHint/errorTitle/banners) + the a11y template.
Telemetry: `view.opened` (screen_view) with surface slug `BatteryHealthAnalyticsWidget` (P1/S11 seam).

