KMP Shared.xcframework (prerequisite for the literal Apple build)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The literal `xcodebuild` scheme runs a pre-build Run Script that stages the KMP `Shared.xcframework`
via Gradle (`:core:assembleSharedXCFramework`). On this checkout the DEBUG xcframework assembles:
  > Task :core:assembleSharedDebugXCFramework
  xcframework successfully written out to: apps/shared/core/build/XCFrameworks/debug/Shared.xcframework
…but the RELEASE Kotlin/Native link (`:core:linkReleaseFrameworkIosArm64`) is the long-pole step and did
not finish under live parallel-slot Gradle/Kotlin-Native contention (7 concurrent konan link processes
observed across slots). Frameworks/Shared.xcframework was therefore never staged. This is the
pre-existing, environmental blocker tracked in apps/macos-pending-verifications.md (KMP scaffold S3-0001),
independent of this surface.

